<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lothar Franz von Schönborn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1655">1655</a>–<a href="/years/1729">1729</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lothar Franz von Schönborn was prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a> from 1693 and archbishop-elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> from 1695 until his death. A great patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architecture, he built the New Residence in Bamberg and the palaces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paide">Weissenstein</a> at Pommersfelden and Gaibach. As arch-chancellor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> he supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and advanced his family's power across the Franconian sees.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lothar-franz-von-schonborn.jpg" alt="Lothar Franz von Schönborn" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christian Schilbach · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurf%C3%BCrst_Lothar_Franz_von_Sch%C3%B6nborn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
